## What's missing

| Gap | Consequence |
|---|---|
| Calibration not versioned or reproducible | The 90%+ claim can't be recomputed or defended when challenged |
| Precision only, no recall | Says nothing about false *positives* — the judge silently passing real failures |
| Golden set grows without version tags | Adding hard cases drops the aggregate and **reads as a regression** when nothing changed |
| No run persistence | Can't answer "did last week's change help?" |
| No repeats | A single judge run is close to meaningless — judges are noisy |
| No uncertainty | Can't distinguish a real improvement from sampling noise |
| Judge noise and system noise conflated | A flaky case could be an unreliable engine *or* an unreliable judge — currently indistinguishable |
| No compare operation | A/B testing impossible despite having versioned prompts |
| No flakiness tracking | Unstable cases are invisible until they embarrass you in a demo |

