## Phase 7 — A/B expansion + retrieval metrics (3–4h)

Two pieces, in this order:

**1. Annotate golden cases with required facts.** For each case, record which node or fact the retrieval must surface for a correct answer. Tedious but mechanical, and it unlocks context recall/precision — the retrieval-level metrics described in Phase 4. This is the highest-value next-week work, above the dashboard.

**2. Sweep.** Run the golden set across *n* configs in one command, produce a ranked table. "I swept retrieval depth and prompt versions and picked the winner on measured pass rate with confidence intervals" is a far stronger sentence than "I tried some prompts."

**Watch for the multiple-comparisons trap.** Sweep ten prompt variants against a noisy metric and the best-looking one is partly winning on luck. Either hold out a second golden subset to confirm the winner, or note the effect explicitly. Naming this problem in an interview is worth more than avoiding it silently.

